# Dry-run publish gate phase 2: Deterministic Generation — Kestrel Toolkit
# release-candidate case study. One domain FRAGMENT of the shared
# kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle domain: this phase's 3 actions chain
# scope-complete -> generate-step1-done -> generate-step2-done -> generate-complete,
# so the merged cycle plan can only reach this phase after Phase 1
# (Release Scope & Identity) completes. 8-constraint split: every
# precondition/effect/goal here is a 1-conjunct (and ...) — far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 — and each action takes 1 parameter
# (PDDL8_MAX_PARAMS=8); the dry-run harness asserts these bounds
# mechanically for every fragment (reusing
# crate::bench::togaf::verify_eight_constraint_split verbatim).
#
# DRY-RUN-OVERCLAIM FENCE: no action effect below is named "published",
# "crates-io-uploaded", or "release-complete" — ggen version pinning, sync
# idempotence, and lock correctness are all LOCAL, REVERSIBLE checks, never
# an external upload. See packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl for the
# full fence disclosure.
#
# Public-ontology doctrine: the artifact node is a blank node; the phase is
# identified by its public SKOS notation. The only private predicate is
# the cng pipeline's ABI carrier ceng:pddlDomain (urn:chatman:engine#),
# disclosed in packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "DRY-RUN-GENERATE" ;
    dcterms:description "Deterministic Generation domain fragment of the kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle STRIPS domain."@en ;
    ceng:pddlDomain """
(define (domain kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle)
  (:requirements :strips)
  (:predicates
    (scope-complete ?x)
    (generate-step1-done ?x)
    (generate-step2-done ?x)
    (generate-complete ?x))
  (:action pin-ggen-version
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (scope-complete ?x))
    :effect (and (generate-step1-done ?x)))
  (:action verify-sync-idempotence
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (generate-step1-done ?x))
    :effect (and (generate-step2-done ?x)))
  (:action verify-lock-correctness
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (generate-step2-done ?x))
    :effect (and (generate-complete ?x))))
""" .
